<%# The navbar's balance seat: the engine user nav's balance_slot, passed where
    layouts/application renders layouts/navbar (/tasks/turf-readopts-engine-navbar).

    The slot holds two mutually exclusive faces:
      [data-balance-display]     the "$1284" wallet link
      [data-free-entry-label]    the "✨ Free Entry" stand-in
    A $0 balance held by a user WITH an entry token reads "✨ Free Entry" instead
    of a redundant "$0": the amount they can enter for is zero dollars, which is
    the point, not an empty wallet. The same rule re-applies live through
    applyBalanceSlotRule() in solana_utils.js after mints and consumes, so the
    server render and the client never drift.

    THE PEEK. The label also peeks over the amount while the ✨ badge on the
    avatar is hovered or focused (.fe-peek), the answer to "what is this
    sparkle?". The badge rides the engine's avatar-badge seat, a sibling of the
    account control, and this slot sits in the icon column, so no Alpine scope
    holds both. The badge dispatches free-entry-peek (true on enter and focus,
    false on leave and blur; components/_entry_token_badge) and this slot's own
    scope listens on the window. %>
<%# display_balance is nil while the navbar cache is cold ("loading"): the
    server no longer blocks the render on the balance RPC. HIDE the whole
    balance link (the "$" too) while loading so there is no lone "$"; the
    client's refreshBalance() then sets [data-balance-display] AND removes
    .hidden, so the full "$112" appears at once. %>
<% balance_loading = display_balance.nil? %>
<% balance_dollars = display_balance.to_f %>
<% balance_zero    = !balance_loading && balance_dollars.zero? %>
<%# Cache-first (display_entry_token_count): nil while cold counts as "no
    tokens", so a real $0 balance is not swapped during loading;
    applyBalanceSlotRule re-applies the swap after hydrate. %>
<% has_tokens      = display_entry_token_count.to_i.positive? %>
<% free_entry      = balance_zero && has_tokens %>
<% hide_balance    = balance_loading || free_entry %>
<div class="relative flex-shrink-0 leading-none mr-1"
     data-balance-slot="true"
     x-data="{ peek: false }"
     @free-entry-peek.window="peek = $event.detail"
     x-bind:class="peek ? 'fe-peek' : ''">
  <%# nav-balance takes its font-size from --nav-p (xl -> lg) instead of a
      reactive class swap. transition-colors keeps the hover fade. %>
  <%= link_to wallet_path, class: "nav-balance dm-blue block font-mono text-primary hover:text-primary-600 dark:hover:text-primary-300 transition-colors duration-300 font-bold leading-none #{'hidden' if hide_balance}", data: { balance_display: true } do %><% unless balance_loading %>$<%= balance_dollars.to_i %><% end %><% end %>
  <%# No size binding: the two faces want DIFFERENT sizes (the peek is a compact
      pill, the stand-in matches the amount it replaces), so .free-entry-label
      and .is-active own font-size in application.css. %>
  <%= link_to wallet_path, class: "free-entry-label dm-blue gap-1 font-bold text-primary hover:text-primary-600 dark:hover:text-primary-300 leading-none whitespace-nowrap #{'is-active' if free_entry}", data: { free_entry_label: true } do %><span class="fe-spark" aria-hidden="true">✨</span><span>Free Entry</span><% end %>
</div>
